language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ de_bruijn_sequence: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A de Bruijn sequence of order n on an alphabet of base symbols is a cyclic sequence in which every possible length-n string over the alphabet occurs exactly once as a substring (read cyclically). Find such a sequence for the given base and order; it has length base^n.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `de_bruijn_sequence.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/de_bruijn_sequence.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `de_bruijn_sequence_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py de_bruijn_sequence.json
$   savilerow model.eprime de_bruijn_sequence_1.param -run-solver

$ base: the size of the alphabet, symbols 0 to base-1
given base : int(1..)
$ n: the order, the length of the substrings
given n : int(1..)
$ seq_len: the length of the sequence, base^n
letting seq_len = base ** n

$ de_bruijn[p]: the symbol at position p of the cyclic sequence (positions 1-based, so the output's first entry is position 1); a value from 0 to base-1
find de_bruijn : matrix indexed by [int(1..seq_len)] of int(0..base-1)

branching on [de_bruijn]
such that
$ each of the base^n length-n strings read cyclically from a start position occurs exactly once: the value of the string starting at each position is different
allDiff([ (sum j : int(1..n) . de_bruijn[((i + j - 2) % seq_len) + 1] * base ** (n - j)) | i : int(1..seq_len) ])
